# Security Rules

## Authentication
- Use Keycloak for authentication
- Protect routes with authentication middleware
- Verify JWT tokens on protected routes
- Log all authentication attempts (success/failure)

## Input Validation
- Validate ALL inputs using express-validator
- Sanitize HTML content using sanitize-html
- Never trust user input
- Validate data types, ranges, formats

## Security Logging
- Log all security events: `logSecurity('event', { context })`
- Include: requestId, userId, ip, userAgent
- Track: auth failures, authorization failures, suspicious activity

## Sensitive Data
- Never log passwords, tokens, or sensitive data
- Redact authorization headers in logs: `[REDACTED]`
- Use environment variables for secrets
- Never commit .env files

## Request Context
- ALWAYS generate request ID: `req.id = 'req-${Date.now()}-${random}'`
- Include requestId in all logs
- Track user context: userId, ip, userAgent

## CORS Configuration
- Configure CORS properly for production
- Use environment variables for allowed origins
- Never use wildcard (*) in production

## Rate Limiting
- Implement rate limiting on all public endpoints
- Use express-rate-limit middleware
- Configure different limits for different endpoints
